  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952; thirteen candidates for twelve seats (Mid-Ulster Mail, 24 May 1952, p. 5). 'Twelve Unionists Had Easy Victory.' Electorate 1,956; 1,616 voted; 33 spoiled votes; poll about 82.2 per cent. Twelve Official Unionists elected and the Independent, Patrick M'Aweaney, defeated. Figures agree with the Belfast News-Letter table, 22 May 1952, p. 5."
